  "site_description": "At Basement Bike Mechanic, all my bicycle repair work happens right here at my basement workshop in Atlanta — you drop your bike off at the shop, and I take care of it from start to finish. I serve Atlanta's cycling community with expert repair, maintenance, and tune-ups designed to keep you riding smoothly and safely. If getting to me isn't convenient, I offer optional collection within 5 miles: I'll pick up and return your bike, but the actual repair work still happens here at the shop (not at your home or on-site). Whether you're a daily commuter, weekend rider, or serious cyclist, you get friendly, professional service in a welcoming environment. From flat tire fixes and brake adjustments to complete overhauls, I handle all types of bikes with care and precision. Ready for a tune-up? I operate exclusively by reservation to give your bike the attention it deserves. Text me or book online to get on the schedule.",
  "regular_maintenance_first": "Regular bicycle tune-ups and proper maintenance are essential for keeping your bike safe, efficient, and enjoyable to ride. A tune-up helps ensure that your brakes and gears are working smoothly, your tires are properly inflated, and all moving parts are clean and well-lubricated, which reduces wear and extends the lifespan of the components. Proper maintenance can prevent costly repairs by catching small issues before they turn into major problems, and it also improves performance, making pedaling easier and rides more comfortable.",
  "regular_maintenance_second": "Beyond saving money and time, a well-maintained bike is safer, giving you reliable stopping power, stable handling, and fewer chances of breakdowns on the road or trail. Whether you ride daily or occasionally, investing in a tune-up keeps your bicycle running at its best and helps you get the most out of every ride.",
  "service_header": "Tune Ups",
